  "question": {
    "text": "A sphere of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is gently dropped into a liquid of viscosity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">η</mi></math> in a vertical uniform tube. It attains a terminal velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></math>. Another sphere of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> when dropped into the same liquid, will attain a terminal velocity",
    "image": null
